From bdd3c2ea2c120c5200f182b1676b860942abc71e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:34:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: mark the excavated vault grid dark, as the comment says

borg_excavate_vault() cleared BORG_GLOW on the grid it had just dug and
then set BORG_GLOW again under a comment reading "Dark" -- BORG_DARK
was almost certainly meant. The freshly dug grid was remembered as
glowing, so glow-driven decisions (resting on lit grids, light-driven
flows) could treat a dark, freshly excavated pocket as safe light.
Set BORG_DARK to match the comment.
---
 src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c b/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c
index 559d06053..bdc8e1a32 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon-util.c
@@ -1096,7 +1096,7 @@ bool borg_excavate_vault(int range)
             /* Not Lit */
             borg_grids[borg_temp_y[i]][borg_temp_x[i]].info &= ~BORG_GLOW;
             /* Dark */
-            borg_grids[borg_temp_y[i]][borg_temp_x[i]].info |= BORG_GLOW;
+            borg_grids[borg_temp_y[i]][borg_temp_x[i]].info |= BORG_DARK;
             /* Feat Floor */
             borg_grids[borg_temp_y[i]][borg_temp_x[i]].feat = FEAT_FLOOR;
             /*
-- 
